  message: "P2 REVIEW 2026-09-25 (dev e4a47383ab). THE RUBY LIMB'S PREMISE IS WRONG; php and elixir hold. Status unchanged.\n\nRUBY: the \"NO SYMBOL\" claim is false today, and it was false at filing.\n- The parity test's own fixture (m.rb = `APP = C.new`), run through the full survey pipeline, emits `ruby:m.rb:1-1:APP:variable`. The direct analyzer call emits it too.\n- The emitter is WI-jusus, 699239d969 (2026-07-13), \"emit kind=field/variable symbols for Ruby data members\". That landed 18 days BEFORE this row (07-31).\n- What Ruby actually lacks is the `constructed_from` meta key: the emitted APP node's meta is {'visibility_signal': 'default'}. So Ruby is the row's OTHER, \"bounded\" shape, KEY MISSING, the same fix the six languages already closed.\n- Consequently the strict-xfail reason for ruby in packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_constructed_from_parity.py (KNOWN_HOLES[\"ruby\"], \"NO SYMBOL (WI-kavam) ... emits no module-level variable/constant symbol\") is a false statement. The cell stays red only because the key is missing, so the xfail still holds for a different reason than the one it states.\n\nPHP, reproduced: `<?php $app = new C();` at file scope emits only the class/file symbols, no variable.\nELIXIR, reproduced: `defmodule M do @app C.new() end` emits only module M.\n\nSuggested re-scope: split Ruby out as a key-stamping fix (and correct the xfail reason in the same PR). php + elixir stay the prerequisite-symbol gap this row describes."  # 45f6
